      "wiki_content": "Director's Cut is a remix album by English singer-songwriter Kate Bush, released on 16 May 2011. It consists of new versions of songs from her earlier albums The Sensual World (1989) and The Red Shoes (1993). All tracks have new lead vocals, drums, and instrumentation and are remixed and restructured. Some song were transposed to a lower key to accommodate Bush's lowering voice. Three of the songs, including \"This Woman's Work\", have been completely rerecorded, often with lyrics changed in places. Bush described the album as a new project rather than a collection of remixes. <a href=\"https://www.last.fm/music/Kate+Bush/Director%27s+Cut\">Read more on Last.fm</a>. User-contributed text is available under the Creative Commons By-SA License; additional terms may apply.",
      "wiki_summary": "Director's Cut is a remix album by English singer-songwriter Kate Bush, released on 16 May 2011. It consists of new versions of songs from her earlier albums The Sensual World (1989) and The Red Shoes (1993). All tracks have new lead vocals, drums, and instrumentation and are remixed and restructured. Some song were transposed to a lower key to accommodate Bush's lowering voice. Three of the songs, including \"This Woman's Work\", have been completely rerecorded, often with lyrics changed in places. Bush described the album as a new project rather than a collection of remixes. <a href=\"https://www.last.fm/music/Kate+Bush/Director%27s+Cut\">Read more on Last.fm</a>."
